{"ts":1793411124806,"who":"dev-a","event":"done","summary":"PLAT-103-1: validateApp throws 'app.owner is required' for missing/empty/non-string owner; shared-contracts bumped 1.0.0->2.0.0 (breaking; PR #2). PLAT-103-2: billing passes owner 'payments' (from package.json team; PR #3), merged, CI+CD green. Assumptions: libs/shared-contracts is inlined at build time (not a registry package), so 'adopting the release' needs no dependency bump; lib-only merge deploys nothing. Landed lib first, then billing. Core shell/reports are dev-b's (PR #1); until those ship, a rebuild of them would fail at startup."}
